<<~ ahu slot=`#/canon-vs-code-collisions`>>

!! Canon vs code collisions

# ''Retire the “store-wall still owed” testimony.''
Canon: M1 calls it outstanding and rank 1 lists its lane in flight. Code: the requested head merges PR #194 and contains inode refusal, launcher enforcement, and nonblocking regular-file validation. (`R:74`, `:49`; `T/module-inodes.mjs:33`; `T/launch-codex.mjs:384`; `T/commit-relay.mjs:56`, `:61`; commit `e1d801042`.)

# ''Retire L24’s “no production writer” claim.''
Canon: no writer appends a renewed `device-edge`, and no door frees the joinee. Code: the root-answer path appends that renewal; stale cached answers still refuse, requiring a fresh request. The lease command also refuses stranding rolls. Keep the remaining qualification work. (`R:671`; `N/commands/device-admit.ts:444`, `:475`, `:476`; `N/commands/persona-lease.ts:119`.)

# ''Reject the advertised bare end-to-end CLI recipe.''
Canon/runbook: Stable founding uses `found --hearth`. CLI help instead advertises bare `rite founding`, then `persona new 0`. Code: bare found creates no seed charter, and persona zero explicitly refuses without one. (`R:1099`; `F:146`; `C/commands/vessel.ts:191`, `:192`; `C/commands/found.ts:112`; `N/commands/init.ts:608`.)

# ''Reject the compound rite’s claim to halt at every failed step.''
Its comment promises first-refusal halting; its loop checks exit codes. `stand` deliberately returns zero for most unsuccessful payloads. (`C/commands/vessel.ts:117`, `:131`; `C/commands/stand.ts:383`, `:435`, `:437`.)

# ''Replace the compound rite’s environment/passphrase explanation.''
Its commentary describes boot class through whether an archive opens and a passphrase reaches the environment. Current boot deliberately starts without custody; TTY credentials reach the live custody frame. (`C/commands/vessel.ts:103`; `N/main.ts:351`, `:476`; `C/custody-prompt.ts:25`; `C/commands/vault.ts:221`.)

# ''Do not treat “the hearth stands” output as M4 qualification.''
The road’s M4 names the operator’s live founding rite; the founding command prints that phrase before instructing the operator to stand the vessel. (`R:78`; `C/commands/found.ts:168`, `:177`.)

# ''Replace `OldShapeRefusal` with the actual refusal.''
Canon names `OldShapeRefusal` before route collection. Code preserves that ordering but names `OccupiedStoreRefusal`. (`R:1258`; `C/commands/found.ts:105`, `:108`.)

# ''Retire older blanket “unwired browser/archive/socket” inventories.''
Older roadmap passages leave socket cutover, signer/archive custody, and the browser custody path absent or unreached. Current code seats peer admission, keeps browser face archives, invokes custody-backed founding, and lifts browser session signing. Remaining completeness work does not erase those callers. (`R:516`, `:526`, `:587`, `:1166`; `N/open-node-vessel.ts:1318`; `V/open-browser-vessel.ts:869`, `:915`, `:953`, `:1727`.)

# ''Replace the ambient `.env` shim diagnosis.''
Canon retains an environment-bleed concern. Current shim explicitly selects its configured env file or `/dev/null` for compose. (`R:1229`; `T/lares-container.sh:66`, `:68`, `:70`.)

# ''Preserve the collision inside recovery direction.''
K22 proposes production recovery wiring around a helper that reconstructs a root. M7 requires contacts to rotate the root and reconstruct nothing. The helper’s source confirms reconstruction. A critical review must resolve that conflict before wiring. (`R:760`, `:80`; `N/recovery-keel.ts:31`, `:45`.)

# ''Resolve the road’s competing test-recut ordering.''
One road passage places test recut before founding; the explicit operator-order passage assigns the later harness/AI batch after standing. Neither establishes a product-code dependency. Prefer the explicit order until the controller trues the carrier. (`R:602`, `:46`.)

# ''Keep targets separate from landed claims.''
M6’s complete lease/version retirement, slice 6 idempotence, and slice 7 pre-bind disclosure remain unmet targets in source. The road itself marks their remaining work; treat them as gaps, without manufacturing a contradiction or claiming present completion. (`R:76`; `BL:105`, `:106`; `N/commands/persona-lease.ts:121`; `W/main.ts:603`.)

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/what-i-could-not-settle`>>

!! What I could not settle

* ''Settle exact-candidate green:'' have the lead provide CI and held-out receipts matching the final SHA. Source inspection proves neither a passing run nor absence of standing load failures. (`T/held-out-cells.mjs:120`, `:130`.)

* ''Settle artifact freshness:'' have the lead perform the final bake/build and compare image revision, genesis manifest/bytes, node/web artifacts, and boot-selected seed. Docker copying committed genesis supplies no fresh-bake proof. (`Dockerfile:60`, `:128`.)

* ''Settle M6 completeness:'' enumerate every authority decision and dyad reader, then inject missing lineage, missing raises, stale replicas, and incomplete frontiers. Require explicit refusal; the lexical lease census alone cannot certify that property. (`K/board-dyad-reader.ts:27`; mesh test `lease-law-census.test.ts:56`.)

* ''Settle crash behavior:'' lead runs kills after atom persistence, after archive/anchor persistence, before bootstrap, and after applying a write without answering it. Compare atom/group identities, causal heads, orphan rows, and duplicate effects. (`BL:105`, `:107`.)

* ''Settle erasure behavior on real phones:'' distinguish a missing keystore with surviving continuity from a fully erased origin; measure both recovery/refusal and named fresh-vessel join behavior. (`V/browser-vessel-identity.ts:331`; `BL:106`.)

* ''Settle L24’s full scope:'' enumerate all current lease-advancing acts and test fresh-request renewal plus the no-operator-answer control. Existing renewal code disproves absence; it does not certify every device’s survival. (`N/commands/device-admit.ts:444`; `N/commands/persona-lease.ts:112`.)

* ''Settle L27/L29 residuals and G56:'' lead runs the named Kahu projection, ward-refusal, dedicated-pagehide, herm-drain, and controlled listener/gate-order witnesses. Each needs live execution beyond this read seat. (`R:677`, `:672`, `:894`.)

* ''Settle household infrastructure:'' the operator/lead must demonstrate trusted HTTPS and DNS on the actual phone, including encrypted-DNS behavior where applicable. This seat neither inspected credentials nor contacted the household. (`R:1281`; compose `:235`.)

* ''Settle the pre-rite/M4 boundary:'' record that a scratch household qualified the final candidate before the live operator re-found. ''INFER:'' this ordering avoids demanding a live household phone join before that household’s first founding; the road separately permits scratch qualification and reserves the operator’s hand act. (`R:646`, `:649`, `:1246`.)

* ''Settle shipped-seed pin interruption:'' lead runs a kill between initialization and pin persistence. Current code permits an unpinned boot, so do not report the pin as an atomic founding guarantee. (`N/commands/init.ts:179`; `N/genesis-resolve.ts:66`, `:77`.)

